WEBVTT

00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:18,400
how can I get rid of uterine fibroids? I have lived with them for a long time, was told

00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:24,720
many years ago that they have calcified. I am not totally uncomfortable with them, but

00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:33,120
I feel they may be the cause of a frequent urination issue I have. I currently use castor

00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:41,600
packs on them and have been told that proteolytic enzymes would help. Is there any rife

00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:55,470
program or protocol that can help get rid of them? Typically uterine fibroids, so a uterine

00:00:55,470 --> 00:01:06,750
fibroid is a non-cancerous tumor in the uterus. If it is active, it can cause issues with size

00:01:06,750 --> 00:01:10,990
occupied lesion. It can cause issues that the person is trying to get pregnant. It can cause

00:01:10,990 --> 00:01:18,430
issues. The most common issue with uterine fibroids is bleeding. If a person has bleeding issues,

00:01:18,430 --> 00:01:30,190
the uterine fibroids could be the cause of anidemia. It is not uncommon that a person with

00:01:30,190 --> 00:01:39,070
uterine fibroids, if they get large enough, can cause anidemia. From a natural perspective,

00:01:39,070 --> 00:01:46,990
how do you get rid of uterine fibroids? First of all, what are the causes of a uterine fibroid?

00:01:47,550 --> 00:01:53,470
Most people believe that it has to do with imbalance in hormones at different times,

00:01:53,470 --> 00:02:03,390
similar to PCOS, but that is just a debate. We don't know fully what they're caused by.

00:02:04,350 --> 00:02:13,230
If they are causing anidemia condition, it's best to get them surgically removed. There is no natural

00:02:13,230 --> 00:02:21,310
quote-a-quote cure for uterine fibroids. I have had people use the cyst program on the right

00:02:21,310 --> 00:02:28,590
with some success. Some people have had no success with it. If the fibroids are not causing issues,

00:02:28,590 --> 00:02:36,270
and again, the most common issue is anidemia because it's gobbling up ironed,

00:02:37,630 --> 00:02:42,430
then you have to get them removed. If they're not causing any issues,

00:02:42,430 --> 00:02:45,950
and you're not having anidemia, and if it's true, it is calcified,

00:02:46,510 --> 00:02:51,070
then you might just leave it alone. I didn't even know if I'd even be doing castoral

00:02:51,070 --> 00:02:56,750
packs on that area. You don't want it to become active. You don't want it to become growing.

00:02:56,750 --> 00:03:02,670
You don't want it to be drawing iron and creating anidemic condition, because then it's a surgical

00:03:02,670 --> 00:03:04,270
situation.

